1
00:00:11,417 --> 00:00:14,099
Fourteen facts that sound wrong, but are
true.

2
00:00:14,849 --> 00:00:18,622
Water expands when it freezes, which is
why ice floats on a lake.

3
00:00:19,172 --> 00:00:23,561
A light-year is the distance light travels
in one year, not a measure of time.

4
00:00:24,111 --> 00:00:27,327
The human body contains about thirty-seven
trillion cells.

5
00:00:27,877 --> 00:00:30,292
Sound cannot travel through the vacuum of
space.

6
00:00:30,842 --> 00:00:34,244
Photosynthesis converts light energy into
chemical energy.

7
00:00:34,794 --> 00:00:38,358
The Earth's core is roughly as hot as the
surface of the Sun.

8
00:00:38,908 --> 00:00:43,900
Antibiotic resistance arises when bacteria
evolve under selective pressure.

9
00:00:44,450 --> 00:00:48,246
A black hole's event horizon is the
boundary beyond which nothing can escape.

10
00:00:48,796 --> 00:00:53,858
Honey never spoils; edible honey has been
found in three-thousand-year-old Egyptian

11
00:00:54,408 --> 00:00:56,916
Octopuses have three hearts and blue
blood.

12
00:00:57,466 --> 00:01:00,194
A day on Venus is longer than a year on
Venus.

13
00:01:00,744 --> 00:01:03,321
Bananas are berries, but strawberries are
not.

14
00:01:03,871 --> 00:01:05,821
Sharks existed before trees.

15
00:01:06,371 --> 00:01:10,121
A teaspoon of neutron star material would
weigh billions of tons.

16
00:01:10,671 --> 00:01:15,141
Which one surprised you? Tell me in the
comments, and follow for more science.

